---
description: Documentation style for Markdown files in this project
globs: "**/*.md,**/*.mdx"
alwaysApply: false
---

When writing or editing documentation:

- Verify every claim against the code and run each documented command before including it.
- Write for a reader who has not seen this code. Put the answer before the background.
- Second person, present tense, one idea per sentence. Cut "simply", "just", "easily".
- Use the exact names from the code and the interface.
- Commands, paths, and option names go in backticks. Code blocks state their language and
  run as written.
- Steps are a numbered list with one action each. Options are a table.
- A README answers, in order: what it is, how to install it, the smallest working example,
  where to go next.
- Changelog entries are grouped as Added, Changed, Fixed, Removed and written for users.
